isoPSV_multiengine v2.0.187 (build 2026-11-19) stage-A spectrum-coverage guard (H99 live verdict), zero output change on the default path (all outputs byte-identical to the 186 chain on the 79,686-spectrum regression and the Example exam): stage A only reads the step-1 cache unlabeled/*.mgf - when psm_file was replaced without rebuilding that cache, every merged spectrum missing from the cache was silently skipped inside the worker (is.na(li) -> next, no log, no product; H99 submitted 518 spectra and got 20 verdicts, 91% with no trace; proven on four arm/round datasets: |target spectra x cache titles| equals the stage-A reported spectra exactly). Three hardenings: (1) a coverage check before scoring - every merged spectrum that must take part (Label-filtered when unlabeled_channel=1) has to be present in the unlabeled/ title set; any gap stops the run, writes stageA_unmatched_spectra.tsv and prints a bilingual repair pointer (delete unlabeled/ and rerun step 1) instead of degrading silently; (2) stage A writes every non-participating spectrum with its reason (not_in_unlabeled_mgf / no_candidate, the latter reported back by the workers) and WARNs; (3) step1_done.txt now carries the psm_file md5+size - on mismatch the marker is invalidated, the stale cache is cleared and the spectra are re-extracted (which is the correct semantics for increment rounds: new spectra require a fresh competitive search); legacy markers adopt the current state so existing projects keep resuming. New 1.unlabeled_result/skipped_spectra.tsv merges the gate-skipped spectra (annotated/novel_skipped) and the stage-A non-participants into one two-column table, so downstream explains "no verdict" from one file instead of inferring it from empty master_table cells; step 1 also records unlabeled/step1_spectra.tsv for audit.
